@startuml
title UML State Chart Diagram

state "Login" as L
L : entry / User logs into the system and selects a destination
L : do / Verification of login credentials
L : exit / Displays journey details upon user login and destination selection

state "Journey Details" as JD
JD : entry / Journey details displayed
JD : do / User can activate driving mode or choose other options
JD : exit / Transitions to Mode Selection State

state "Mode Selection" as MS
MS : entry / User activates driving mode or chooses other options
MS : do / User is in driving mode if driving activated
MS : exit / Transitions to Driving State if driving activated, to Eating Option State (optional) upon user detection of hunger

state "Driving" as DR
DR : entry / User is in driving mode
DR : do / System detects an accident or user reports one
DR : exit / Transitions to Accident State if an accident is detected or reported, to Notification State upon sending notifications during driving or in case of an accident

state "Accident" as AC
AC : entry / System detects an accident or user reports one
AC : do / Informs relevant authorities
AC : exit / Transitions to [*] if recovered from, to Logout State upon user logout

state "Notification" as NT
NT : entry / System sends notifications during driving or in case of an accident
NT : do / Notification sent
NT : exit / Transitions to Driving State

state "Eating Option" as EO (optional)
EO : entry / User can select a place to eat if they are hungry
EO : do / User views the menu of the selected eating place
EO : exit / Transitions to Order Placement State (optional) upon user placing an order

state "Order Placement" as OP (optional)
OP : entry / User places an order
OP : do / Order placed
OP : exit / Transitions to [*]

state "Feedback" as FB
FB : entry / User provides feedback upon completion of their journey
FB : do / Feedback submitted
FB : exit / Transitions to [*]

state "Logout" as LO
LO : entry / User logs out of the system
LO : do / Logout event
LO : exit / Transitions to [*]

@enduml
